  "observations": [
    "Actually inspected fresh blink singleton and both four-gesture source sheets at native size on light and dark mattes. Orange/cream facial mask and central forehead stripe, oval white-surrounded brown eyes, paired rounded ears/forepaws/feet, and one thick curled tail remain connected and uncut. No extra limb, dirty paint or background cloud seen.",
    "At inherited max430 the quiet blink keeps neutral crown/chin/torso/paws/feet and tail placement close. Greeting, left/right gaze and forepaw presentations, cheek think/aha and two-arm cheer are distinct and clean. Compact torso/head scale and foot support stay coherent.",
    "Species pair changes only the existing tail curve/tip with grounded body, and returns toward ordinary tail. All seven decoded static sequence rows inspected in both mattes; no obvious body-scale pop or missing part apparent."
  ],
